WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:08.383
BEN: Hello, Little Fox Readers, and welcome to a new edition of People in the

2
00:00:08.384 --> 00:00:15.962
News . Today Olivia will be introducing us to Xi Jinping, president of China

3
00:00:15.963 --> 00:00:19.871
and leader of the Chinese Communist Party. He heads the country with the largest population

4
00:00:19.872 --> 00:00:26.027
in the world. OLIVIA: You’re right, Ben. More than 1.4 billion people call China home.

5
00:00:26.028 --> 00:00:31.858
That means that almost one of every five people on earth lives in China! Xi

6
00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:39.692
was born in 1953, in Beijing. His father was a high-ranking member of the

7
00:00:39.693 --> 00:00:45.341
Communist Party. The third of four children, Xi grew up in a world of privilege

8
00:00:45.342 --> 00:00:53.427
in Beijing. Along with the sons of other important Communist Party members, he was known

9
00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:57.933
as a "princeling," or young prince. Xi attended an elite school with these other princelings.

10
00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:06.068
Their school was sometimes even called the "cradle of leaders," because of the students’

11
00:01:06.069 --> 00:01:15.920
very powerful and influential families. But Xi’s life changed dramatically in the 1960s when his

12
00:01:15.921 --> 00:01:18.989
father fell out of favor with Chairman Mao Zedong and was arrested. His mother was

13
00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:25.572
forced to work on a farm. The Red Guard, young supporters of Mao, threatened Xi

14
00:01:25.573 --> 00:01:35.805
and made him renounce his father. Later, as part of Mao’s Cultural Revolution, many

15
00:01:35.806 --> 00:01:41.630
upper-class students were sent to rural areas to be "reeducated" by the peasants. This meant

16
00:01:41.631 --> 00:01:48.200
that the students were expected to learn about life from a peasant’s point of view.

17
00:01:48.201 --> 00:01:55.613
At the age of 16, Xi was sent to work on a farm in Shaanxi

18
00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:59.794
province. Out of shape, Xi was not prepared for the intense manual labor or

19
00:01:59.795 --> 00:02:05.029
the rough living conditions. His back-breaking work included shoveling manure! At night he slept on

20
00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:11.424
a kang , a bed made of bricks and clay. Xi said later that he

21
00:02:11.425 --> 00:02:20.514
was miserable there—he hated the fleas, the food, and the work. After three months Xi

22
00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:27.092
ran away, but he was arrested and sent back to the farm, where he

23
00:02:27.093 --> 00:02:32.510
worked for about six years. It was a difficult time in Xi’s life, but today

24
00:02:32.511 --> 00:02:36.991
he credits this experience with transforming him. He says it gave him a new appreciation

25
00:02:36.992 --> 00:02:42.998
for farmers and the poor. BEN: Wow. Did Xi ever have the chance to return

26
00:02:42.999 --> 00:02:48.487
to school? OLIVIA: Yes, in 1975 he was allowed to leave the farm to

27
00:02:48.488 --> 00:02:55.080
study chemical engineering. He graduated from Beijing’s Tsinghua University in 1979. Studying part-time, he later

28
00:02:55.081 --> 00:03:01.572
earned a law degree from the same university in 2002. Although some princelings wanted nothing

29
00:03:01.573 --> 00:03:07.071
more to do with the Communists, Xi was eager to join the party. His application

30
00:03:07.072 --> 00:03:14.721
was rejected seven times while his father was still out of favor. But in

31
00:03:14.722 --> 00:03:21.530
1974 his application was accepted, thanks to the influence of a local party member. When

32
00:03:21.531 --> 00:03:25.979
Mao died in 1976, Xi’s father went back to work for the party. Xi landed

33
00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:30.038
his first job after college with his father’s help. He became secretary to China’s vice-premier.

34
00:03:30.039 --> 00:03:36.195
The vice-premier is part of China's State Council, a powerful branch of the government.

35
00:03:36.196 --> 00:03:41.129
With this important job, Xi began his rise through the Communist Party. By 2000 he

36
00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:45.444
was governor of Fujian province. Seven years later he became a member of the politburo,

37
00:03:45.445 --> 00:03:51.855
the committee that rules the party. In 2008 he was elected vice-president of China. In

38
00:03:51.856 --> 00:03:56.280
March 2013 the National People’s Congress, China’s legislature, elected Xi president of China. BEN:

39
00:03:56.281 --> 00:04:05.424
What does Xi want to accomplish as president? OLIVIA: Xi would like to make China

40
00:04:05.425 --> 00:04:08.429
the world’s most powerful nation. He often uses the slogan "China Dreams" to describe a

41
00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:13.092
brighter future for his country and its people. China already has one of the fastest-growing

42
00:04:13.093 --> 00:04:20.259
economies in the world. But Xi would like to see it improve even more.

43
00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:24.749
Xi has also pledged to improve everyone’s state of living. He would like to be

44
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.918
seen as a friend of the poor and a man of the people. He wants

45
00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:32.335
to fight corruption within the government too. This has been a serious problem in China

46
00:04:32.336 --> 00:04:37.744
for many years. The military is very important to Xi too. He wants China

47
00:04:37.745 --> 00:04:45.658
to become a major military power. He has increased the destructive power of China’s nuclear

48
00:04:45.659 --> 00:04:52.571
weapons. He has also built artificial islands in the South China Sea that can be

49
00:04:52.572 --> 00:04:57.234
used for military bases. As president, though, Xi faces many challenges. Air pollution is a

50
00:04:57.235 --> 00:05:04.455
big problem in China, and people are beginning to demand changes. The economy’s growth

51
00:05:04.456 --> 00:05:08.549
has benefited China, but it’s also created an income gap. Many people have grown wealthy,

52
00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:14.379
while others remain quite poor. Some nations, such as the United States, have criticized China

53
00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:24.295
for not being more concerned about human rights. And the artificial islands in the South

54
00:05:24.296 --> 00:05:31.627
China Sea have sparked tense disputes over territory. BEN: Hmm . . . Those

55
00:05:31.628 --> 00:05:38.945
do sound like challenging issues. What can you tell us about Xi’s family? OLIVIA: His

56
00:05:38.946 --> 00:05:45.269
first marriage ended in divorce. He then married Peng Liyuan, a well-known folksinger, in 1987.

57
00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:53.604
They have a daughter, who graduated from Harvard University in the United States. Oh, and

58
00:05:53.605 --> 00:05:59.014
Xi is a fan of American movies. He also likes to read, swim, and

59
00:05:59.015 --> 00:06:03.090
watch sports on TV, although he has very little free time. Unlike some previous leaders,

60
00:06:03.091 --> 00:06:09.921
Xi is very popular with the Chinese people. He is even known as "Papa Xi."

61
00:06:09.922 --> 00:06:17.685
After he ate at a Beijing fast-food restaurant in 2014, the place became a huge

62
00:06:17.686 --> 00:06:25.494
tourist attraction. People crowd the restaurant to eat the same meal Xi enjoyed: steamed

63
00:06:25.495 --> 00:06:33.573
buns and pig liver stew. At a college, art students had to draw Xi’s picture

64
00:06:33.574 --> 00:06:39.732
as part of their entrance exam. His photo is everywhere and a book of his

65
00:06:39.733 --> 00:06:48.289
philosophies is a best seller. There are even a number of songs about him! BEN:

66
00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:56.552
Thanks for the informative report, Olivia. I bet the world will be watching to

67
00:06:56.553 --> 00:07:02.254
see how Xi Jinping leads China into the future! See you soon, Little Fox readers.

